# This repository denies by default and permits by exception.
#
# The usual shape is the opposite: track everything, list what to exclude. That
# is the wrong default here. This repository will hold paths to DICOM and NIfTI
# volumes and to PPMI tables held under a data use agreement, and the cost of
# the two mistakes is not symmetric. Forgetting to exclude a file publishes it,
# permanently, because git history has no clean undo. Forgetting to include one
# produces an error message at the moment you try to add it.
#
# So: `*` denies everything, the `!` lines below permit the handful of file
# kinds this project legitimately contains, and the final section re-denies
# anything that would otherwise slip through a permit.
#
# **If `git add` refuses a file you meant to track**, that is this file working.
# Add a permit for it deliberately, and check first whether the file describes
# the project or the person. Two files were committed here that described the
# person: a personal task list and the local paths, cache size and version of
# an installed vendor binary. Neither belonged in a public repository.
#
# This is the first of two layers. `git add -f` overrides everything here, so
# `.githooks/pre-commit` re-checks what is actually staged. Neither layer has
# an override.

# --- deny everything ---------------------------------------------------------
*

# Descend into directories, otherwise the permits below are unreachable.
!*/

# --- permit: source and tests ------------------------------------------------
!*.py

# --- permit: documentation ---------------------------------------------------
!*.md

# --- permit: project configuration -------------------------------------------
!pyproject.toml
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.githooks/pre-commit
!.claude/settings.json

# Fixture data is permitted at the very bottom of this file, not here. A permit
# placed above the `*.csv` denial below would be overridden by it, silently.


# =============================================================================
# RE-DENY. Everything below overrides the permits above, because gitignore
# resolves later rules last. Order matters: these must stay at the bottom.
# =============================================================================

# --- environments and caches -------------------------------------------------
# Without these, `!*.py` above would happily track every file in a virtualenv.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# --- personal working notes --------------------------------------------------
# Task lists naming applications, schedules or people are working notes, not
# project documentation. The site repository applies the same rule to
# znatodos.md.
TASKS.local.md
*.local.md
human-tasks.md
docs/human-tasks.md
NOTES.md
TODO.md

# --- participant data, in any form -------------------------------------------
# Redundant against `*` above and kept anyway. If someone later adds a permit
# for a directory or an extension, these still hold, because they are last.
data/
Data/
DATA/
dicom/
DICOM/
raw/
ppmi/
PPMI/
naps/
NAPS/
dpuk/
DPUK/
cohorts/
participants/
derivatives/

*.dcm
*.DCM
*.ima
*.IMA
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.img
*.hdr
*.mhd
*.mha
*.raw
*.nrrd
*.nhdr
*.v
*.par
*.rec
*.minc
*.mnc

# Archives hide all of the above.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar

# Tabular participant data. PPMI ships clinical and binding-ratio tables as
# CSV; loaders take a path from config and the tables live outside the repo.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.sav
*.dta

# --- trained weights ---------------------------------------------------------
# A model trained on participant-level PPMI data may only be shared through
# routes MJFF approves. Code ships MIT; weights do not ship.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.h5
*.pkl
*.joblib
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
loni_*.txt

# --- editor and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- permit: narrow, reviewed fixtures ---------------------------------------
# Last, because a permit only beats a denial written above it. One fixture at a
# time, with a reason, never by wildcard. A fixture must be synthetic and small
# enough for a reviewer to read in full.
#
# `.githooks/pre-commit` carries the matching exception, so the two layers
# agree on exactly one allowed path shape.
!tests/fixtures/synthetic_*.csv
